  "raw_text": "\n\nBrowse Program Information\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAcademic Program:\tB.Sc. in Biomedical Sciences\nAcademic Year:\t2024\nLanguage:\t\nEnglish\nSimplified Chinese\nTraditional Chinese\n\n\n\nLearning Outcomes\nStudy Scheme\n \n\n\t\n\nBiomedical Sciences\n\nApplicable to students admitted in 2024-25\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\nMajor Programme Requirement\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\nStudents are required to complete a minimum of 70 units of courses as follows:\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\nUnits\n\n\n\n\n1.\n\n\t\n\nFaculty Package:\n\n\t\n\n10\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nMEDF1011, 1021, 1031, 1041, SBMS1102\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n2.\n\n\t\n\nRequired Courses:\n\n\t\n\n28\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nSBMS1101, 1103, 2101, 2102, 2104, 2105, 2106, 2107, 2108, 3101, 3105\n\n\t\n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n3.\n\n\t\n\nElective Courses:\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n(a)\n\n\t\n\nStudents must choose only one Concentration Area from the following:\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nConcentration Area A: Biomedical Research[d]\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n(i)\n\n\t\n\nSBMS3201, 4201[e], 4202[e]\n\n\t\n\n8\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n(ii)\n\n\t\n\n6 units of courses chosen from the following:\n\n\t\n\n6\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\nSBMS3202, 3203, 3204, 3205, 3206\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nConcentration Area B: Strategic Management and Entrepreneurship\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n(i)\n\n\t\n\nEPIN1020#, 2010#, 3020# or 3021# or 3022#, LAWS2331#, SBMS3215, 3216\n\n\t\n\n14\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n(ii)\n\n\t\n\n1 course chosen from the following:\n\n\t\n\n1\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\nSBMS4203, 4204\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nConcentration Area C: Health Services and Consultation\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n(i)\n\n\t\n\nSBMS3207, 3208, 3209, 3210, 3211\n\n\t\n\n13\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n(ii)\n\n\t\n\n1 course chosen from the following:\n\n\t\n\n1\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\nSBMS4203, 4204\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n(b)\n\n\t\n\n17-18[a] units of courses chosen from the following[b]:\n\n\t\n\n17-18\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nEPIN1020#, 2010#, 3020# or 3021# or 3022#, LAWS2331#, PHAR3420#, SBMS2201, 3201, 3202, 3203, 3204, 3205, 3206, 3207, 3208, 3209, 3210, 3211, 3212, 3213, 3214, 3215, 3216, 4203[c], 4204[c], 4205[c]\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nTotal:\n\n\t\n\n70\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nExplanatory Notes:\n\n\n\n\n1.\n\n\t\n\nAll SBMS courses as well as those labeled as # will be included in the calculation of Major GPA for honours classification.\n\n\n\n\n[a]\n\n\t\n\nStudents who choose Concentration Area B are required to take 17 units of elective courses, while those choosing other Concentration Areas should take 18 units of elective courses.\n\n\n\n\n[b]\n\n\t\n\nCourses taken to fulfill requirement 3(a) cannot be counted towards the fulfillment of requirement 3(b).\n\n\n\n\n[c]\n\n\t\n\nOnly for students choosing Concentration Area B or C.\n\n\n\n\n[d]\n\n\t\n\nConcentration Area A students, who opt for the CUHK-UoM Study Option and have successfully completed 180 credits of modules in Master of Science in Infection Biology or Master of Science in Tissue Engineering for Regenerative Medicine offered by the Faculty of Biology, Medicine and Health, The University of Manchester, will be granted course and unit exemptions for up to 18 units of Major Elective Courses.\n\n\n\n\n[e]\n\n\t\n\nCapstone courses\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nRecommended Course Pattern\n\n\t\n\nUnits\n\n\n\n\nFirst Year of\n\nAttendance\n\n\t\n\n1st term\n\nFaculty Package: 3 courses\n\nMajor Required: SBMS1101, 1103\n\nMajor Elective(s):\n\n\t\n\n \n\n5\n\n5\n\n\n\n\n2nd term\n\nFaculty Package: 2 courses\n\nMajor Required: SBMS2105\n\nMajor Elective(s):\n\n\t\n\n \n\n5\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSecond Year of Attendance\n\n\t\n\n1st term\n\nMajor Required: SBMS2101, 2102, 2107\n\nMajor Elective(s):\n\n\t\n\n \n\n8\n\n\n\n\n2nd term\n\nMajor Required: SBMS2104, 2106, 2108\n\nMajor Elective(s):\n\n\t\n\n \n\n8\n\n\n\n\nThird Year of Attendance\n\n\t\n\n1st term\n\nMajor Required: SBMS3101\n\nMajor Elective(s): 6-9 units of courses\n\n\t\n\n \n\n2\n\n6-9\n\n\n\n\n2nd term\n\nMajor Required: SBMS3105\n\nMajor Elective(s): 7-10 units of courses\n\n\t\n\n \n\n2\n\n7-10\n\n\n\n\nFourth Year of Attendance\n\n\t\n\n1st term\n\nMajor Required:\n\nMajor Elective(s): 9-12 units of courses\n\n\t\n\n \n\n \n\n9-12\n\n\n\n\n2nd term\n\nMajor Required:\n\nMajor Elective(s): 10-13 units of courses\n\n\t\n\n \n\n \n\n10-13\n\n\n\n\nTotal (including Faculty Package):\n\n\t\n\n70\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\nCourse List\n\n\n\n\nCourse Code\n\n\t\n\nCourse Title\n\n\t\n\nUnit(s)\n\n\n\n\nSBMS1101\n\n\t\n\nBiomedical Sciences and Society\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS1102\n\n\t\n\nHuman Structure and Function\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS1103\n\n\t\n\nBiochemistry of Human Body\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS2101\n\n\t\n\nBiostatistics and Epidemiology\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS2102\n\n\t\n\nIntroduction to Molecular Biology\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS2104\n\n\t\n\nIntroduction to Bioethics\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS2105\n\n\t\n\nLaboratory Techniques in Biomedical Sciences\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS2106\n\n\t\n\nPharmacology and Toxicology\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS2107\n\n\t\n\nHuman Functions and Diseases I\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS2108\n\n\t\n\nHuman Functions and Diseases II\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS2201\n\n\t\n\nNatural Product Pharmacognosy and Drug Development\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3101\n\n\t\n\nImmunology\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3105\n\n\t\n\nMicrobiology\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3201\n\n\t\n\nExperimental Design and Execution, Journal Analysis and Reporting Results\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3202\n\n\t\n\nCancer Biology\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3203\n\n\t\n\nDevelopmental Biology and Reproductive Medicine\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3204\n\n\t\n\nNeuroscience\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3205\n\n\t\n\nStem Cell and Regenerative Medicine\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3206\n\n\t\n\nCardiovascular and Metabolic Biology\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3207\n\n\t\n\nIntroduction to Good Manufacturing Practice for Advanced Therapy Medicinal Products\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3208\n\n\t\n\nForensic Science\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3209\n\n\t\n\nClinical Anatomical Pathology\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3210\n\n\t\n\nInstrumental Analysis and Application in Biomedical Sciences\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3211\n\n\t\n\nMolecular Techniques in Genetics and Medicine\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3212\n\n\t\n\nBioinformatics, Genomics and Proteomics\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3213\n\n\t\n\nDrug Design and Development\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3214\n\n\t\n\nMedical Genetics\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3215\n\n\t\n\nThe Landscape of the Biomedical Industry\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS3216\n\n\t\n\nHealth Services Management\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSBMS4201\n\n\t\n\nCapstone Research Project I\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS4202\n\n\t\n\nCapstone Research Project II\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nSBMS4203\n\n\t\n\nBiomedical Internship I\n\n\t\n\n1\n\n\n\n\nSBMS4204\n\n\t\n\nBiomedical Internship II\n\n\t\n\n1\n\n\n\n\nSBMS4205\n\n\t\n\nBiomedical Internship III\n\n\t\n\n1\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\nStudy Scheme\n\n\nLearning Outcomes\n \n\n\t\n\n1.      Major Programme\n\n\n\n\nUpon completion of the Programme, the graduates will have:\n\n\n\n\n1. demonstrated good knowledge and understanding of\n\n\n\n\n·         anatomy, biochemistry, pharmacology, physiology, molecular biology, medical genetics, etc. and selected advanced areas of biomedical sciences (i.e. specialized topics);\n\n·         human diseases – pathophysiology, pathology, diagnosis and genetic counseling;\n\n·         biomedical laboratory techniques and related safety procedures;\n\n·         biostatistics and research methods;\n\n·         ethical and legal issues in biomedical science;\n\n·         healthcare system and pharmaceutical management;\n\n·         legal perspectives on intellectual property. \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n2. acquired practical skills to\n\n\n\n\n·         perform a wide range of biomedical laboratory techniques competently;\n\n·         know how to make use of a range of modern information technologies;\n\n·         organize data and ideas for effective presentations using a variety of formats (e.g. oral, poster);\n\n·         work effectively and cooperatively within a group.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n3. acquired cognitive/thinking skills to\n\n\n\n\n·         interpret and critically evaluate laboratory data;\n\n·         critically review scientific literature;\n\n·         develop own ideas through critical appraisal and integration of known concepts, principles and published literature;\n\n·         design a research project, collect, analyze, interpret and evaluate research data; recognize, analyze and respond to the moral, ethical and social issues related to advances in biomedical science knowledge and research;\n\n·         recognize advances and future development in biomedical sciences from local, regional and global perspectives.\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n4. acquired skills to\n\n\n\n\n·         formulate a career development plan;\n\n·         demonstrate an autonomous and reflective approach to experiential and lifelong learning;\n\n·         demonstrate literacy, numeracy and problem-solving skills;\n\n·         apply knowledge and skills to career development in education, management, laboratory-based services, postgraduate studies or research in biomedical sciences and related clinical or healthcare-related disciplines.    \n\n \n\n \n\n\n"
